<title>USA: U.S. Sen leader Lott says hopeful on tax cuts.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sen leader Lott says hopeful on tax cuts.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senate Majority Leader Trent Lott said Wednesday discussions with President Clinton and Democrats showed there was reason for optimism that tax cuts would be agreed by the two sides.</p>
<p>&quot;I think we have been moving toward each other,&quot; the Mississippi Republican said in a speech to the National Association of Manufacturers.</p>
<p>He noted that Democrats have now proposed some capital gains relief for farmers and small businesses, which puts them closer to the Republican position.</p>
